  "releaseNotes": "- Condition editor: a null-value condition on a field that does not offer the is-empty / is-not-empty search modes is no longer misdetected as the is-empty mode. Previously such a condition (e.g. built by a field-specific search control) lost its value editor and was rewritten to a broken shape when saved.\n- Condition editor: the target field list now also offers fields reached through links - row fields of embedded 1:N list fields (\"Members.Status\"), scalar fields on linked modules (\"Department.Manager\"), and row fields of list fields defined on linked modules (\"Department.Members.Role\"). Selecting such a path shows the search UI of the resolved field (including enum value candidates), and the resulting condition is evaluated as the corresponding link-hop reference. Sort keys and comparison variables also offer linked-module scalars.\n- Code-defined design enums (C# enums marked with the DesignEnum attribute) appear in the solution tree, the enum editor, and the EnumName candidates like ordinary design enums, but are read-only in the editor and excluded from rename refactoring and file saves (the C# definition is the source of truth).",
